decapitation it's pretty simple it's the  total separation of the head from the  body  this includes a complete severing of 26  muscles  four major blood vessels the spinal  column and most importantly  the spinal cord which by the way  regulates a multitude of motor  sensory and autonomic functions in  contrast  internal decapitations only involve the  separation of the spinal cord from the  base of the skull  but the neck is still attached to the  body the exact cause of death in a  decapitation  is technically severing of the spinal  cord and rapid blood loss  and that's all there is to know about  the anatomy of decapitation  however i'm willing to bet you clicked  on this video with something else in  mind  not just how you die from a decapitation  but also if your severed head is still  conscious  well that's what the rest of the video  covers and by referencing scientific  experiments and reliable data there  certainly is an answer  but first a shout out to the sponsor of  this video babel  if you're watching this then chances are  you're not decapitated which means your  brain is still working just fine but you  know what they say  if you don't use it you lose it and  that's where babel comes in babel is the  number one language learning app in the  world with over 14 different  languages a 2012 study from the dana  foundation  showed that being bilingual helped  participants process information more  efficiently  improved memory and enhanced visual  spatial skills or  maybe you're like me and you're  traveling abroad so you have to learn a  new language in a pinch  babel can teach you a new language in  just three weeks with 10 to 15 minute  lessons a day  you'll go from sounding like this excuse  me server  waiter anybody to this  excuse me in fact studies have shown  that 15 hours of babble is commensurate  with the semester of college spanish  classes are constructed by 150 real  language teachers  giving you real words and phrases you'll  actually use in addition to traditional  learning  babel offers different methods of  learning as well such as podcasts  interactive games and more  babble has a very special offer of 65  off  click the link in the description for  more information a deal this good  is a no-brainer the question of  consciousness after decapitation  is one people have wondered for  centuries considering that the visual  auditory scent and even touched senses  in the brain are not directly affected  by decapitation  it's theoretically possible for  consciousness to remain intact  oh by the way severed heads cannot talk  i didn't mean to scare you because  there's no vocal cords attached  anyways only the brain stem is directly  affected in decapitation  so with these regions being untouched it  could lend possible consciousness  historically the most famous alleged  instance of consciousness  after decapitation was the execution of  charlotte corday  during the french revolution corday had  murdered french journalist and  politician  jean-paul marat she was tried found  guilty  and sentenced to public execution by the  guillotine  after she was decapitated the  executioner's assistant francois legro  lifted her head for the crowd to see and  slapped it  eyewitnesses claimed they saw cordee's  face blush  and show a look of anger at legro but  eyewitness accounts are not reliable  data  especially as scientific data what the  crowd believed to be consciousness was  likely reflexive facial nerves firing  away in a severed head  however post-decapitation facial  movements historically have been cited  as  proof of consciousness but these only  exist in non-scientific historical  records and are more folklore than  anything else  however history is not completely void  in this case  there was one scientific experiment  known to observe  human consciousness after decapitation  in 1905.  french physician dr gabriel barrow was  given permission to conduct experiments  on a prisoner  set for execution the prisoner henry  langu was executed on june 28  1905 for murder the guillotine dropped  and langu's head  fell dr barrow grabbed the severed head  immediately to begin the experiment  holding langu's severed head he began to  speak to it  the following is what he recorded in his  medical journal  i was able to note immediately after the  decapitation the eyelids and lips of the  guillotine man  worked in irregularly rhythmic  contractions for about five or six  seconds  the spasmodic movement ceased it was  then i called in a strong sharp voice  langu i saw the eyelids slowly lift up  without any spasmodic contractions i  insist  quite distinct and normal such as  happens in everyday life  with people awakened or torn from their  thoughts dr barreaux repeated this two  more times  and allege the head responded each time  though it sounds astounding  no observations have ever been  referenced from other physicians or  scientists nor has the experiment been  published in an accredited medical  journal  language reactions were likely delayed  reflexes  or barrow may have over exaggerated his  observations out of excitement  but this only generates more questions  than it does answers  what is the baseline for consciousness  does the severed head have to be  blinking or show  facial or mouth movements to be  conscious what if what appears to be an  expressionless severed head  is actually a being with full  consciousness this question was tested  by a team of dutch and french scientists  in 2011. in the study decapitation in  rats  latency to unconsciousness and the wave  of death the electrical activity of rap  brains was measured using an eeg  or electroencephalography both before  and after decapitation  ideally the readings would show normal  electrical activity then decapitation  followed by either continued electrical  output or none at all  the eeg is the best measurement of  consciousness after decapitation  because if there's no electrical  activity in the brain  i.e no neurons firing how can you be  conscious and aware  two groups of rats were used one group  was conscious before decapitation  and the other was made unconscious using  anesthetics  since the unconscious group would be  producing unconscious brain waves before  decapitation the scientists could use  this to compare to the post-decapitation  brain waves to determine if they were  truly conscious  or unconscious here are the results  there's many graphs and tables from the  experiment and i could go through every  single  one and bore you on all the details but  no the only graph that really matters to  us  is this one right here the red dots and  lines signify the unconscious or  anesthetized wraths and the blue lines  and dot signifies the conscious or awake  rats immediately after decapitation  which is this dotted line right here the  electrical activity in the brain drops  very quickly within 10 seconds similar  to a battery that loses its charge  when the brain loses electrical activity  it cannot power  all of its different functions one of  these functions being  sensory input according to the eeg the  cognitive activity in the wrap brain  that maintains  sensory input such as sight smell  hearing and pain  dropped below 50 3.7 seconds  after decapitation a decrease of 50  percent  in cognitive activity means the rat's  brain cannot maintain consciousness  this means that during those 3.7 seconds  after decapitation  sensory input continued and therefore  there was consciousness  however after four seconds consciousness  was completely lost  and within 20 seconds the brain produced  zero electrical activity  which can be seen as a flat line on this  eeg reading  there you have it what turned out to be  gory folklore turned out to be  gory reality if you ever find yourself  beneath the guillotine or an  executioner's axe  be sure to take a good look around  because afterwards those three or four  seconds are going to be your last
 

